==Strategy==
With the stage entirely consisting of [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemies, it's best to bring a lineup consisting largely of [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|Meatshields]] and [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|Cats with anti-Dark abilities]]. Some excellent anti-Dark candidates include [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], and [[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]]. For Tackey, fast attackers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] as well as [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] are good options against him. If you have him, [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] can serve as a ranged version of Bombercat.

==Trivia==
*Soap Scum's Japanese name uses some wordplay that was lost in translation. 垢い敵、黒い汗 ''Akai Teki、Kuroi Ase'' literally translates to "Grimy Enemy, Black Sweat", but 垢 ''aka'' (grime) also sounds identical to 赤 ''aka'' (red), so when saying the stage name out loud, it sounds like "[[:Category:Red Enemies|Red Enemy]], Black Sweat".

